<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Argentine National Anthem</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">words adopted 11 May <a href="/years/1813">1813</a>; music composed May <a href="/years/1813">1813</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Himno Nacional Argentino</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">After the May Revolution of 1810, poets and musicians in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> wrote a number of patriotic songs. The earliest, a &quot;Patriotic March&quot; published anonymously on 15 November 1810 in the Gazeta de Buenos Ayres, is generally believed to have words by Esteban de Luca and music by Blas Parera; it did not mention <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> or any independent state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/argentine-national-anthem.jpg" alt="Argentine National Anthem" width="330" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown (Illustration) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Versión_francesa_del_Himno_argentino.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
